cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PRISMA: A Python Toolkit for Systematic Literature Reviews"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Javier"
    family-names: "Cuervo"
    email: "javier.cuervo@proportione.com"
    affiliation: "Universidade de Aveiro (DEGEIT, DBI) and Proportione, LDA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7134-2894"
  - given-names: "Rui Pedro Figueiredo"
    family-names: "Marques"
    email: "ruimarques@ua.pt"
    affiliation: "Universidade de Aveiro (ISCA-UA, GOVCOPP)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Proportione/prisma"
url: "https://proportione.com/investigacion"
abstract: >
  PRISMA is a modular Python toolkit for systematic literature reviews,
  covering corpus ingestion (OpenAlex, RIS), cross-source deduplication,
  title-abstract screening, full-text extraction with PyMuPDF, MMAT 2018
  quality assessment, PRISMA 2020 flow diagrams, and bibliometric analysis
  (cluster detection, keyword co-occurrence, VOSviewer integration). It
  ships a Streamlit demo and a CLI for reproducible reviews.
keywords:
  - systematic literature review
  - PRISMA 2020
  - MMAT 2018
  - bibliometrics
  - meta-analysis
  - research synthesis
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
